      "id": "fill-component-space-transforms",
      "name": "FillComponentSpaceTransforms",
      "category": "SkinnedAsset",
      "signature": "FillComponentSpaceTransforms(Target, In Bone Space Transforms, In Fill Component Space Transforms Required Bones, Out Component Space Transforms)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "USkinnedAsset*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Bone Space Transforms",
          "type": "TArray<FTransform>&"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Fill Component Space Transforms Required Bones",
          "type": "TArray<FBoneIndexType>&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Out Component Space Transforms",
          "type": "TArray<FTransform>&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Take the BoneSpaceTransforms array (translation vector, rotation quaternion and scale vector) and update the array of component-space bone transformation matrices (ComponentSpaceTransforms).\nIt will work down hierarchy multiplying the component-space transform of the parent by the relative transform of the child.\nThis code also applies any per-bone rotators etc. as part of the composition process"
    },
    {
      "id": "get-detailed-info-internal",
      "name": "GetDetailedInfoInternal",
      "category": "SkinnedAsset",
      "signature": "GetDetailedInfoInternal(Target)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "USkinnedAsset*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "String",
      "docs": "This will return detail info about this specific object. (e.g. AudioComponent will return the name of the cue,\nParticleSystemComponent will return the name of the ParticleSystem)  The idea here is that in many places\nyou have a component of interest but what you really want is some characteristic that you can use to track\ndown where it came from."
    },
